  "surprise": "Discard: 635 (634/622/649) vs 153-claude's 687 (676/700/685), -52, below the pre-registered floor of -35. Every mechanism prediction landed inside its band: n_params 9,578,784 exactly; steps 3,881/3,880/3,930 (3.43-3.48 epochs; -14% vs 153's 4,540/4,479/4,489, predicted 3,700-4,400); final val 0.0845/0.0843/0.0786, equal or lower than 153's 0.088/0.087/0.089; greedy 0.960/0.969/0.958 (153: 0.9675/0.967/0.968); RL sampling 222-269 samples/s (>= 200); totals 1,717/1,724/1,825 s. Yet the RL start was worse on every seed: round-1 targets solved 684/726/688 vs 153's 766/747/694 (r1 sample acc 0.228/0.271/0.254), round-4 1,127/1,095/1,140 (mean 1,121 vs 1,157). That is exactly the pre-registered mechanism falsifier (equal-or-lower val loss with a lower RL start on all three seeds): the gate bought pretraining fit, not the conditional features the RL start needs. Surprise: the metric gap (-52) is larger than the r1 gaps for seeds 1 and 2 imply, so the gated MLP also improved less per RL round (r4 +9 to +12 fewer per seed at similar sample accuracy 0.69-0.72); and the 14% fewer steps cannot carry it alone (124-claude's narrower GELU MLP at D 256 was null). Parameter-matched SwiGLU at hidden 856 is a worse handoff than GELU 1280 here; P23 closed at this width and param cap. A FLOP-unmatched retry (SwiGLU at 1280 hidden) would pass the 10M cap at D 384, so it would need a narrower trunk and is not worth a slot.",
